{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/236987-tips-for-creating-a-great-character","id":236987,"title":"Tips for creating a great character","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-21T15:29:55-07:00","id":236987,"title":"Tips for creating a great character","content":"I'm a huge fan of Mummy: the Curse but haven't yet had the privilege to be a player in a Mummy Chronicle. This inexperience as a player led to an awkward moment the other day when I was trying to sell one of my friend on Mummy and they asked me the million dollar question: &quot;How can you make a fleshed out character when they can barely remember who they are?&quot;<br /> <br /> I tried to explain how an Arisen's Decree, Guild, Judge, and Cult all hint at their true nature but they're convinced that they just reinforce the character's archetype and not their background and personality. I was about to hit the old Core book again but though it might be quicker and more thought provoking to ask the forum their opinions on the matter. Can anyone give some advice about creating a great character for Mummy: the Curse so if nothing else I can at least show my friend you can make a character who isn't just an archetype in Mummy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T09:01:27-07:00","id":237041,"title":"","content":"Well, they still have a Virtue and Vice: that will determine a great deal of their personality alone (have your character pursue their First Task, Decree, Virtue, and Vice single-mindedly, and simultaneously). There's also the Cult. A Cult's rituals, behaviors, and general attitude toward a Mummy will shape what kind of person the Mummy is at low Memory. Granted, a lot of that will probably be ego-swelling what with all of the worship and kowtowing.<br /> <br /> Finally, and this requires Storyteller help, how does a Mummy react to Sekhem loss and resets? Especially Sekhem loss due to certain behavior. That will help them understand their Judges' plan for them, but what if they don't like the direction the Judge seems to be pointing? Say a Mummy does something nice for someone, but then suffers Sekhem loss. How would that make the Mummy feel? Would your Arisen take the opportunity to help somebody again in the future after that?<br /> <br /> Finally, remember that Mummy is a game of discovering who your character was. Starting the game, you won't have a good idea of who your character is. In that way, it's sort of like every Descent is a chance to be a <i>new</i> person, rather than the one you were.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm of the opinion that a truly great character only manifests during play, and no matter how interesting or well-written the backstory, it's a poor substitute for characterisation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T15:39:35-07:00","id":237471,"title":"","content":"This is why I hit the forums instead of the books, thank you <b>BigDamnHero</b> I was so hoping for an angle I hadn't seen yet and you presented several brilliantly. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure if I'll be able to sell my friend on how great Mummy: the Curse is but now I can at least explain that the Arisen are more than just archetypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T15:35:56-07:00","id":238623,"title":"","content":"At Memory 3, a character remembers their past Descent. Players should be fine to decide what happened there. When pitching it to a player who really likes to design their character's history, ask them to think of it this way. Your character has lived many, many lives. You can decide what the most recent one was like. The rest are a mystery, but you still effectively have a single Arisen lifetime (so to speak) to write up. Every dilemma, event, emotional crisis, and defining moment that could be used to create a great character normally can easily be set into that most recent Descent, especially when coupled with the eternal and never-changing elements like the character's Decree and Judge.<br /> <br /> So, basically, think of it less like losing control of your backstory, and more like the GM creates background elements to layer on top of a backstory you get to create. You do have holes in your memory, most important of those being that you can't remember your origins, but it doesn't mean you have no sense of who your character is. That previous descent can be used to create all the depth and complexity you could ever want in your character, and then you get to begin play.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, I didn't have much of a problem with this aspect of the game when pitching it to my group. Most of my players rarely write more than 2-3 paragraphs of background information for their characters anyway, and only one of my players found the loss of control over their character a little bit troubling. They came around pretty quickly with the above explanation. After all, it's how you actually play the character that counts, and in Mummy the GM has the ability to challenge you on a roleplaying level by not just presenting you with a crisis in the present, but also by showing you how you dealt with such events in the past. And if your present character disagrees with his own past decisions... well, that's just when the real fun begins, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T17:21:24-07:00","id":238699,"title":"","content":"That does remind me, do an Arisen's Affinities and Utterances transfer over from Descent to Descent? And if so then under what circumstances would a Mummy find themselves in the 21st century with the states of a starting character? Does it work something alongst the lines of: &quot;The more successful you are in serving the Judges the more stronger you'll be when you next arise.&quot; Or is it purely up to the Storyteller?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T00:35:31-07:00","id":238930,"title":"","content":"Affinities are built into a Mummy's soul and so presumably carry over from Descent to Descent, but as written have plenty of reasons to go dormant, be liquidated, or otherwise disappear.<br /> <br /> Utterances, on the other hand, are rote magic that have to be studied. It is presumably quite easy to have and later lose access to an Utterance.<br /> <br /> In either case, there are a variety of reasons why a starting character might &quot;only&quot; have the powers they begin with, and lots of fun reasons for why a character might demonstrate abilities in flashbacks that they don't possess in their current life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T02:02:39-07:00","id":238957,"title":"","content":"Thanks again for the advice and rules clarifications. I just have one last technical question: are the seven dots you get for merits separate for the ten dots each for the Cult and Tomb merit? That was the only part about character creation that I didn't quite understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T22:54:47-07:00","id":239945,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what you're talking about there, honestly. I started my players off with 7 merit dots. What's this about ten dots for Cult and Tomb?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T23:22:55-07:00","id":239956,"title":"","content":"Ah, I must have just misread the instructions then. Never mind, I have no further questions. Thanks again <b>Azahul</b> and <b>BigDamnHero</b> for you help, it's greatly appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T20:09:42-07:00","id":241928,"title":"","content":"Actually, I think I found the part you are talking about. Page 157, Unpacking the Cult Merit sidebar, talks about getting ten free points to spend on Reach, Grasp, and benefits. I don't think it's mentioned in the actual character creation section (I dunno, has been a little while since I read it), and I don't think the example of character creation involves it, but it's not a bad idea. If you do decide to use that rule, then they are presumably separate from the seven merit dots you get at character creation.<br /> <br /> I'm going to blame the fact that I'm using a different in-game method of Cult management in my game for why that part didn't stick in my brain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T06:09:48-07:00","id":242201,"title":"","content":"Azahul: That is an irritatingly-placed sidebar that would have greatly improved the two games of Mummy I've been in so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T17:13:21-07:00","id":242679,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I know. I would probably have given my players a stronger starting Cult if I'd realised that was the norm.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, it shouldn't be a big deal in my game. It could probably serve to be a bit more prominent during character creation though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}